      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WILLOWS GIRL (2) is a talented filly who was good enough to overcome a wide barrier for a resuming win at this venue. She should be better for the outing and she has the speed to take full advantage of the low draw so will be tough to stop. RIPPLES NZ (7) is back from a hit-and run trip to NZ where she came from a wide barrier for third at Alexandra Park. That was her first outing since she came from the back row to win July's Queensland Oaks. May need a bit of luck negotiating a very wide starting position but she is tough. PRE EMINANT (6) is a consistent filly who added to a string of top-two results when she came from the back row for second in the Vicbred final. She can be in the finish again. DELIZIOSO (1) was first up for 11 months when she came from a wide barrier to miss narrowly fresh. Fitter and is aided by the ace draw.",
